\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Event signal accumulation. Each article contributes a decaying signal with magnitude $s_k$ and rate $\lambda _k$. The aggregate is the sum of the active article kernels. Curves illustrate the mechanism and are not empirical parameter estimates; the horizontal scale and the displayed rates use hours. The model is inspired by Hawkes-type kernels but does not fit a self-exciting arrival intensity.\relax }}{7}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:decay_stacking}{{2}{7}{Event signal accumulation. Each article contributes a decaying signal with magnitude $s_k$ and rate $\lambda _k$. The aggregate is the sum of the active article kernels. Curves illustrate the mechanism and are not empirical parameter estimates; the horizontal scale and the displayed rates use hours. The model is inspired by Hawkes-type kernels but does not fit a self-exciting arrival intensity.\relax }{figure.caption.3}{}}
